From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:00:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 224/225] PCI: qcom: Reset the MSM8996 controller each time it
 is set up

Nothing resets the MSM8996 (2.3.2) controller: its init only turns on the
supplies and clocks, and its GDSC stays on across system suspend. That is
fine at probe, but not after a system suspend that powered the endpoint
off (D3cold). On a Samsung Galaxy Tab S3 with a QCA6174:

- after PME_Turn_Off and L2 the link never trains again (LTSSM stays in
  Detect.Quiet, "Device not found"), whether the endpoint lost power or
  not;
- without PME_Turn_Off the link trains, but the endpoint never completes
  a configuration request (all ones, "Unable to change power state from
  D3hot to D0, device inaccessible"), not even seconds later.

Pulsing the controller's block reset before setting it up again fixes
both: the link comes back in L0, ath10k resumes and Wi-Fi reconnects, over
repeated suspends. Take an optional "core" reset and pulse it whenever the
controller is set up, at probe and at resume, like the downstream driver
does on every enable.

Signed-off-by: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
index b58a607b7..4890f21a3 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -215,6 +215,7 @@ struct qcom_pcie_resources_2_3_2 {
 	struct clk_bulk_data *clks;
 	int num_clks;
 	struct regulator_bulk_data supplies[QCOM_PCIE_2_3_2_MAX_SUPPLY];
+	struct reset_control *rst;
 };
 
 #define QCOM_PCIE_2_3_3_MAX_RESETS		7
@@ -719,6 +720,10 @@ static int qcom_pcie_get_resources_2_3_2(struct qcom_pcie *pcie)
 		return res->num_clks;
 	}
 
+	res->rst = devm_reset_control_get_optional_exclusive(dev, "core");
+	if (IS_ERR(res->rst))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(res->rst), "Failed to get core reset\n");
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -743,6 +748,25 @@ static int qcom_pcie_init_2_3_2(struct qcom_pcie *pcie)
 	struct device *dev = pci->dev;
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Nothing else resets the controller: its GDSC stays on across system
+	 * suspend. After the endpoint has been powered off, the controller
+	 * left as it was neither trains the link again (after PME_Turn_Off)
+	 * nor completes configuration requests to the endpoint.
+	 */
+	ret = reset_control_assert(res->rst);
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_err(dev, "cannot assert core reset\n");
+		return ret;
+	}
+	usleep_range(1000, 1500);
+	ret = reset_control_deassert(res->rst);
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_err(dev, "cannot deassert core reset\n");
+		return ret;
+	}
+	usleep_range(1000, 1500);
+
 	ret = regulator_bulk_enable(ARRAY_SIZE(res->supplies), res->supplies);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_err(dev, "cannot enable regulators\n");
